WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.490 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  throughout the day supporters and  opponents of abortion faced off in front  of Colombia's highest court pro-choice  activists hope magistrates would give  women the right to terminate pregnancies  of up to 16 weeks in the end the court  chose to leave abortion laws as they are  but at the same time we are happy that  the lawsuit that attend to take away our  rights was not successful there are  three grounds for abortion in Colombia  opponents say they already go too far  article 11 of the Constitution says life  should never be dishonoured but there  are deranged people who support these  shameful reasons no more no more  the latest debate rose from a case  seeking a return to a total ban after  the court allowed abortion in three  instances in 2016 if the mother's life  is at risk if the fetus is malformed or  in case of rape but even in these cases  many obstacles remain for women to  access the procedure especially if  they're poor or live in rural areas  despite the restrictions health  authorities say that at least 400,000  women terminates their pregnancies every  year here in Colombia most of them do so  illegally and in many cases suffer  serious health consequences human rights  professor Luce Angela Gomez is one of  them she sought an abortion when she was  17 at any legal clinic getting a  dangerous infection as a result or  shion's happen and will keep happening  illegally even in three legal cases  women face undue delays and obstacles  and often resort to unsafe options  facing more problems and even death the  latest case has intensified an already  fierce debate in the country over the  legal and moral implication of abortion  which both sighs promise to keep  fighting for  Alessandra MPT al-jazeera Bogota

